<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Frost Death Knight DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 1. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Heroic Dungeons, reputations and professions.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Frost Death Knight DPS in Phase 1</span></h2>Frost <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s will need to reach the <i>spell hit cap</i> which effects our abilites in Cataclysm Classic.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit Rating - You will want a total of <i>at least</i> +8% chance to hit. This means you'll want at least 961 hit rating in total. There are no longer any buffs or debuffs from your raid to influence your hit rating, so you need to make sure you're sorted from gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - Strength is the primary base stat for <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s, and is always good to get more of. It gives 2 attack power per point, before modifiers are applied.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Attack Power, Critical Strike Rating, Mastery Rating, and Haste Rating all blend together as stats that are desireable, but with lower value than Strength. If you choose to go the "Masterfrost"-route, which this guide focuses on, you'd generally want to get as much Mastery as you can, without being at the expense of Strength</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise Rating - Expertise is a mediocre stat for <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s. It reduces the chance that your and auto attacks, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=49020/obliterate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_classicon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obliterate</span></a>  and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=49143/frost-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_empowerruneblade2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Strike</span></a> will be dodged or parried. When they do, you get you runes refunded, meaning the penalty is very small.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">
<span class="c6">Valor Points for Frost Death Knight DPS Phase 1</span></h3>Valor Points are the new main currency, that can be obtained with a weekly cap of 1600 from doing raids and heroic dungeons. You spend this on your tier pieces, as well as various off-piece items and trinkets. When using this currency, you should consider your personal goals as well as those of your guild. There is not really a single solution that is optimal for every player. As thus, you should make your own assessment and not follow this list blindly. If you aren't planning on progressing difficult heroics early on, you can save up your Valor Points and spend  them on Tier instead, as this will have more longevity than an item like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58180/license-to-slay">
<img alt="License to Slay" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">License to Slay</span></a>, or be more impactful than a weak item such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64674/relic-of-aggramar">
<img alt="Relic of Aggramar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Aggramar</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Should you have an alt doing Heroics or a lot of gold, you can also simply buy <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58195/woe-breeders-boots">
<img alt="Woe Breeder's Boots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Woe Breeder's Boots</span></a> on said character and send them to your <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>, as they are BoE.<br/>
<br/>
