<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="sigils-for-frost-death-knight-dps">Sigils for Frost Death Knight DPS</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64674/relic-of-aggramar">
<img alt="Relic of Aggramar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Aggramar</span></a> is the clear winner, but might be hard to obtain if you are limited on <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>s, as trinkets are more important to get, making the Sigil-slot the least impactful of all. If you played Wrath, you'd know that we used the same sigil for the entirety of the expansion. Fortunately, that is no longer the case, as Sigils have now been reduced to pure stat-sticks, without a significant damage bonus to our abilities.<div class="pad"></div>
